 evidence:['Queensland Autism Hub describes visual supports as resources that make information more accessible. It recommends checking understanding of symbols and simplifying the format when needed. Displaying pictures alone is insufficient. [visual]', 'The EEF includes modelling and temporary scaffolds among inclusive teaching approaches. Support should address an observed barrier without assuming all autistic children learn in the same way. [eef]'],
